<section class="page-hero page-hero--legal">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--center">Trust &amp; Safety</span>
    <h1 class="page-hero__title">Security at <%= site.name %></h1>
    <p class="page-hero__lead">
      Our approach to security starts with a simple idea: the safest way to handle your documents
      is to never send them to us at all. Here is how the platform is built.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="security-grid">

      <article class="security-card">
        <span class="security-card__icon" aria-hidden="true"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'protect' }) %></span>
        <h2>Processing stays in your browser</h2>
        <p>
          The tools run entirely on your device. When you open a file, it is read and processed
          locally — it is not uploaded to our servers, and we never see or store its contents.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="security-card">
        <span class="security-card__icon" aria-hidden="true"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'sign' }) %></span>
        <h2>No document storage on our side</h2>
        <p>
          Because your files never reach us, there is no server-side document database to breach.
          Your working copy lives in your browser and is discarded when you close the tab.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="security-card">
        <span class="security-card__icon" aria-hidden="true"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'convert' }) %></span>
        <h2>Encrypted connections (HTTPS)</h2>
        <p>
          In production, the site is served over HTTPS, so traffic between your browser and the
          website is encrypted in transit using TLS.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="security-card">
        <span class="security-card__icon" aria-hidden="true"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'organize' }) %></span>
        <h2>Strict Content Security Policy</h2>
        <p>
          The app ships a strict Content Security Policy and other security headers to reduce the
          risk of cross-site scripting and code injection. Scripts run only from our own domain.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="security-card">
        <span class="security-card__icon" aria-hidden="true"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'split' }) %></span>
        <h2>No third-party trackers by default</h2>
        <p>
          Fonts and application code are served from our own domain, and we do not load third-party
          analytics or tracking scripts by default. Advertising cookies are used only with consent
          where required.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="security-card">
        <span class="security-card__icon" aria-hidden="true"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'compress' }) %></span>
        <h2>A small, focused server</h2>
        <p>
          Our server’s job is deliberately limited: it delivers the website and application files.
          It has no document-processing endpoints, which keeps the attack surface small.
        </p>
      </article>

    </div>

    <div class="security-note prose">
      <h2>What we don’t claim</h2>
      <p>
        We believe security should be described honestly. No online service can promise to be
        “100% secure,” and we don’t. We don’t use marketing phrases like “military-grade encryption,”
        and we don’t hold certifications we haven’t earned. What we can say is specific and true: your
        files are processed in your browser and are not uploaded to or stored by <%= site.name %>.
      </p>
      <h2>Reporting a vulnerability</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe you have found a security issue, we would genuinely like to hear from you.
        Please email <a href="mailto:<%= site.contactEmail %>"><%= site.contactEmail %></a> with the
        details so we can investigate. For more on data handling, see our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
